From 5024d7e1e81c277182e80d4af8b14d6a2108a0ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ond=C5=99ej=20=C5=A0imon?= <ondrej@dorhawk.software>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:17:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: Restore a background window a window tool tiles
 without activating it.

From Codex's review of Broyojo/hadron#182. A window tool sets every
window's frame without activating the app; the restore once a frame
settles went through SC_RESTORE, whose SW_RESTORE activates, so a
maximized window behind another of the same program took activation
from it. Only the window in front takes SC_RESTORE now; any other is
restored with SW_SHOWNOACTIVATE.

Measured with own-frame hold-maximized second and a tool's left half at
192 DPI: before, the window behind was activated and the one in front
deactivated; after, neither, with the same restored frame. The
single-window case is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/winemac.drv/window.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
index 9cfe104b55..cac6ca662a 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
@@ -2019,8 +2019,12 @@ void macdrv_window_frame_settled(HWND hwnd)
          * dragged or snapped: it comes between WM_ENTERSIZEMOVE and WM_EXITSIZEMOVE, so a program
          * that saves its placement at the end of one hears it. */
         send_message(hwnd, WM_ENTERSIZEMOVE, 0, 0);
-        /* restored now, not when a posted command arrives, to place it below */
-        if (!(NtUserGetWindowLongW(hwnd, GWL_STYLE) & WS_DISABLED))
+        /* restored now, not when a posted command arrives, to place it below. A window tool may
+         * arrange a window in the background: only the one in front takes the title bar's
+         * restore, which activates it; any other is restored where it is. */
+        if (hwnd != NtUserGetForegroundWindow())
+            NtUserShowWindow(hwnd, SW_SHOWNOACTIVATE);
+        else if (!(NtUserGetWindowLongW(hwnd, GWL_STYLE) & WS_DISABLED))
             send_message(hwnd, WM_SYSCOMMAND, SC_RESTORE, 0);
 
         /* Restored, the window has the title bar and borders of a window that isn't maximized, on
